narrative:
## Building a Game Score System

Game scoring has a few core operations: adding points, checking if a score is a new high score, and displaying the scoreboard.

### Adding Points

```xiom
fn add_score(current: Int, points: Int) -> Int {
  return current + points;
}
```

### Checking for High Score

```xiom
fn check_high_score(score: Int, high_score: Int) -> Bool {
  return score > high_score;
}
```

### Displaying the Scoreboard

```xiom
fn display_scoreboard(name: Str, score: Int) {
  io.println("=== SCOREBOARD ===");
  io.println("Player: " + name);
  io.println("Current score updated!");
}
```

### Putting It All Together

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let player = "Kilo";
  var score = 0;
  var high_score = 1000;

  score = add_score(score, 250);
  score = add_score(score, 500);
  score = add_score(score, 400);

  if check_high_score(score, high_score) {
    high_score = score;
    io.println("New high score!");
  }

  display_scoreboard(player, score);

  return 0;
}
```

Three focused functions create a complete scoring loop: accumulate points, compare against the record, display results.

